All positives end with “c b”. Every “c” must be followed by “b”. Between two “c”s the segment may be:
- an odd number of ‘a’s (e.g., acb, aaacb);
- any number of ‘a’s possibly followed by a ‘b’ (e.g., aabcb, bcb);
- any number of ‘a’s, then a ‘b’ or ‘c’, optionally an ‘a’, then “c b” (e.g., cbaa b acb).  
These three possibilities repeated any number of times (including zero) generate exactly the positive strings and exclude the negatives.

